1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,976
Sweetheart, the mantel is the first thing

2
00:00:02,976 --> 00:00:05,662
anybody sees when they walk into your

3
00:00:05,662 --> 00:00:07,476
living room at Christmas.

4
00:00:07,656 --> 00:00:09,096
It's the stage.

5
00:00:09,276 --> 00:00:11,542
And most people treat it like a

6
00:00:11,542 --> 00:00:11,981
shelf.

7
00:00:12,161 --> 00:00:14,204
They line up a row of little

8
00:00:14,204 --> 00:00:16,467
things, stick a garland on top,

9
00:00:16,467 --> 00:00:17,853
hang the stockings,

10
00:00:17,853 --> 00:00:20,043
and wonder why it looks like a

11
00:00:20,043 --> 00:00:22,378
yard sale instead of a magazine.

12
00:00:22,558 --> 00:00:25,626
I've decorated mantels for sixty years,

13
00:00:25,626 --> 00:00:28,222
and it takes about ten dollars to

14
00:00:28,222 --> 00:00:28,537
fix.

15
00:00:28,886 --> 00:00:31,541
So tonight I'm giving you seven Christmas

16
00:00:31,541 --> 00:00:34,131
mantel mistakes that make it look cheap,

17
00:00:34,131 --> 00:00:36,721
and the old-fashioned fixes that make it

18
00:00:36,721 --> 00:00:38,534
look like it cost a fortune.

19
00:00:38,714 --> 00:00:39,908
And stay with me,

20
00:00:39,908 --> 00:00:42,084
because the last one is a trick

21
00:00:42,084 --> 00:00:45,032
my mother used with candlelight that makes

22
00:00:45,032 --> 00:00:47,488
any mantel look beautiful at night,

23
00:00:47,488 --> 00:00:49,454
even if you do nothing else.

24
00:00:49,803 --> 00:00:52,102
Our house on Elm Street had a

25
00:00:52,102 --> 00:00:55,113
little painted wood mantel over a coal

26
00:00:55,113 --> 00:00:57,649
stove that didn't even work as a

27
00:00:57,649 --> 00:00:58,441
fireplace.

28
00:00:58,621 --> 00:00:59,859
But every December,

29
00:00:59,859 --> 00:01:02,008
my mother turned it into the most

30
00:01:02,008 --> 00:01:03,962
beautiful thing on the street.

31
00:01:04,142 --> 00:01:07,076
She used pine branches from the woods,

32
00:01:07,076 --> 00:01:09,470
pinecones Danny and I gathered,

33
00:01:09,470 --> 00:01:11,555
red apples from the cellar,

34
00:01:11,555 --> 00:01:14,335
and her mother's brass candlesticks.

35
00:01:14,515 --> 00:01:15,711
That's it.

36
00:01:15,891 --> 00:01:18,321
And people stopped on the sidewalk to

37
00:01:18,321 --> 00:01:19,897
look through our window.

38
00:01:20,246 --> 00:01:22,637
One year, nineteen fifty-four,

39
00:01:22,637 --> 00:01:26,224
the newspaper sent a photographer around town

40
00:01:26,224 --> 00:01:27,897
for a Christmas page.

41
00:01:28,077 --> 00:01:30,200
He walked past the big houses on

42
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:33,384
Park Avenue with their store-bought decorations,

43
00:01:33,384 --> 00:01:35,705
and he knocked on our door instead.

44
00:01:35,885 --> 00:01:38,402
My mother's mantel was in the Mansfield

45
00:01:38,402 --> 00:01:40,660
News Journal on December twentieth,

46
00:01:40,660 --> 00:01:42,790
and she kept that clipping in her

47
00:01:42,790 --> 00:01:44,790
Bible for the rest of her life.

48
00:01:44,970 --> 00:01:47,205
In a minute I'll tell you her

49
00:01:47,205 --> 00:01:47,745
secret.

50
00:01:48,094 --> 00:01:50,850
Her secret was that she didn't buy

51
00:01:50,850 --> 00:01:52,471
anything new, honey.

52
00:01:52,651 --> 00:01:54,560
She looked at what she had,

53
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:56,680
and she arranged it with care.

54
00:01:56,860 --> 00:01:59,205
That's what most people skip.

55
00:01:59,385 --> 00:02:01,033
They buy more and more,

56
00:02:01,033 --> 00:02:03,253
and they never take the time to

57
00:02:03,253 --> 00:02:04,041
arrange it.

58
00:02:04,221 --> 00:02:06,648
Every mistake I'm going to show you

59
00:02:06,648 --> 00:02:09,422
tonight can be fixed with things already

60
00:02:09,422 --> 00:02:11,780
in your house and the woods behind

61
00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:11,988
it.

62
00:02:12,337 --> 00:02:13,928
Mistake number one.

63
00:02:14,108 --> 00:02:17,011
Lining everything up in a straight row,

64
00:02:17,011 --> 00:02:18,499
all the same height,

65
00:02:18,499 --> 00:02:19,541
like soldiers.

66
00:02:19,721 --> 00:02:21,823
Your eye has nowhere to go.

67
00:02:22,003 --> 00:02:24,342
The fix is to build a triangle,

68
00:02:24,342 --> 00:02:25,625
or a gentle wave.

69
00:02:25,805 --> 00:02:28,351
Put your tallest thing on one end,

70
00:02:28,351 --> 00:02:29,625
or in the middle,

71
00:02:29,625 --> 00:02:32,620
and let everything step down from there.

72
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:35,975
Tall candlesticks, a medium lantern,

73
00:02:35,975 --> 00:02:38,269
a small bowl of pinecones.

74
00:02:38,449 --> 00:02:40,326
Your eye travels across,

75
00:02:40,326 --> 00:02:42,048
and it looks designed.

76
00:02:42,397 --> 00:02:44,273
And use odd numbers,

77
00:02:44,273 --> 00:02:44,836
honey.

78
00:02:45,016 --> 00:02:48,382
Three candlesticks, not two or four.

79
00:02:48,562 --> 00:02:51,175
Five pinecones, not six.

80
00:02:51,355 --> 00:02:53,547
I don't know why it works,

81
00:02:53,547 --> 00:02:54,559
but it does.

82
00:02:54,739 --> 00:02:57,376
My mother said even numbers look like

83
00:02:57,376 --> 00:02:58,517
a store display,

84
00:02:58,517 --> 00:03:00,869
and odd numbers look like a home.

85
00:03:01,049 --> 00:03:03,510
She was right about most things.

86
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:05,911
Here's how to do it in five

87
00:03:05,911 --> 00:03:06,519
minutes.

88
00:03:06,699 --> 00:03:09,021
Take everything off your mantel.

89
00:03:09,201 --> 00:03:10,200
Everything.

90
00:03:10,380 --> 00:03:11,645
Wipe it clean.

91
00:03:11,825 --> 00:03:14,589
Then put back only your tallest piece

92
00:03:14,589 --> 00:03:16,905
first, on the left third of the

93
00:03:16,905 --> 00:03:18,698
mantel, not dead center.

94
00:03:18,878 --> 00:03:20,968
Then put a medium piece on the

95
00:03:20,968 --> 00:03:21,386
right.

96
00:03:21,566 --> 00:03:23,977
Then fill in with small things,

97
00:03:23,977 --> 00:03:26,233
low and close to the garland.

98
00:03:26,413 --> 00:03:28,538
Step back to the door and look.

99
00:03:28,718 --> 00:03:30,575
Move one thing.

100
00:03:30,755 --> 00:03:31,835
Look again.

101
00:03:32,015 --> 00:03:34,267
That's all decorators do.

102
00:03:34,617 --> 00:03:36,324
Mistake number two.

103
00:03:36,504 --> 00:03:37,874
A skinny garland.

104
00:03:38,054 --> 00:03:40,654
One thin strand of fake pine lying

105
00:03:40,654 --> 00:03:42,948
flat on a mantel looks sad and

106
00:03:42,948 --> 00:03:43,406
cheap.

107
00:03:43,586 --> 00:03:45,305
The fix is to layer.

108
00:03:45,485 --> 00:03:48,062
Lay down your cheap garland first,

109
00:03:48,062 --> 00:03:50,488
then tuck real cuttings into it.

110
00:03:50,668 --> 00:03:52,920
Pine, cedar, a little holly,

111
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:55,894
even branches from the bottom of your

112
00:03:55,894 --> 00:03:57,100
Christmas tree.

113
00:03:57,280 --> 00:03:59,130
It makes it full and fat,

114
00:03:59,130 --> 00:04:01,498
and the real ones make the whole

115
00:04:01,498 --> 00:04:03,422
room smell like Christmas.

116
00:04:03,772 --> 00:04:06,160
And let it hang over the ends,

117
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:07,035
sweetheart.

118
00:04:07,215 --> 00:04:09,483
Don't stop the garland right at the

119
00:04:09,483 --> 00:04:10,779
edges of the mantel.

120
00:04:10,959 --> 00:04:13,059
Let it drape down a foot or

121
00:04:13,059 --> 00:04:14,304
so on each side,

122
00:04:14,304 --> 00:04:15,626
like a waterfall.

123
00:04:15,806 --> 00:04:18,692
That's the difference between a garland that

124
00:04:18,692 --> 00:04:21,250
looks like an afterthought and one that

125
00:04:21,250 --> 00:04:23,086
looks like it belongs there.

126
00:04:23,266 --> 00:04:25,608
Tie it down with fishing line,

127
00:04:25,608 --> 00:04:26,935
so nothing shows.

128
00:04:27,284 --> 00:04:29,096
Mistake number three.

129
00:04:29,276 --> 00:04:31,261
Too many little things.

130
00:04:31,441 --> 00:04:34,531
Every ornament, every snow globe,

131
00:04:34,531 --> 00:04:36,684
every figurine you own,

132
00:04:36,684 --> 00:04:38,651
all crowded together.

133
00:04:38,831 --> 00:04:40,469
It looks cluttered,

134
00:04:40,469 --> 00:04:42,453
and nothing stands out.

135
00:04:42,633 --> 00:04:44,096
Pick one idea,

136
00:04:44,096 --> 00:04:44,723
honey.

137
00:04:44,903 --> 00:04:46,819
All brass and greenery.

138
00:04:46,999 --> 00:04:48,914
All white and silver.

139
00:04:49,094 --> 00:04:50,882
All red and wood.

140
00:04:51,062 --> 00:04:53,212
Put the rest away for next year,

141
00:04:53,212 --> 00:04:55,428
and the mantel will look calm and

142
00:04:55,428 --> 00:04:55,764
rich.

143
00:04:56,115 --> 00:04:57,922
If this is helping you,

144
00:04:57,922 --> 00:05:00,045
tap the like button for me,

145
00:05:00,045 --> 00:05:00,909
sweetheart.

146
00:05:01,089 --> 00:05:03,934
It helps Grandma more than you know.

147
00:05:04,114 --> 00:05:05,855
And here's my rule.

148
00:05:06,035 --> 00:05:08,257
If you can count more than eleven

149
00:05:08,257 --> 00:05:10,343
separate things on your mantel,

150
00:05:10,343 --> 00:05:11,353
take three off.

151
00:05:11,533 --> 00:05:12,403
Go ahead.

152
00:05:12,583 --> 00:05:14,151
Count yours tonight.

153
00:05:14,331 --> 00:05:16,397
I'll bet you have twenty.

154
00:05:16,577 --> 00:05:18,689
I'll tell you in a minute where

155
00:05:18,689 --> 00:05:21,210
those extra things should go instead.

156
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:24,051
Here's a little trick for anything you

157
00:05:24,051 --> 00:05:26,018
love that didn't make the cut.

158
00:05:26,198 --> 00:05:28,079
Make a Christmas tray.

159
00:05:28,259 --> 00:05:30,673
A big wooden cutting board or a

160
00:05:30,673 --> 00:05:33,400
silver tray, with your snow globes,

161
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:34,646
a little candle,

162
00:05:34,646 --> 00:05:36,593
and a few sprigs of pine,

163
00:05:36,593 --> 00:05:39,787
all grouped together on the coffee table.

164
00:05:39,967 --> 00:05:42,898
Grouped together, little things look like a

165
00:05:42,898 --> 00:05:43,648
collection.

166
00:05:43,828 --> 00:05:46,382
Scattered, they look like clutter.

167
00:05:46,562 --> 00:05:48,501
Same things, honey.

168
00:05:48,681 --> 00:05:49,981
Different home.

169
00:05:50,331 --> 00:05:52,014
Mistake number four.

170
00:05:52,194 --> 00:05:54,353
Forgetting the wall above the mantel.

171
00:05:54,533 --> 00:05:57,389
Your mantel is only half the picture.

172
00:05:57,569 --> 00:05:59,358
Hang a wreath above it,

173
00:05:59,358 --> 00:06:01,302
or lean a big mirror or a

174
00:06:01,302 --> 00:06:03,247
framed picture behind it.

175
00:06:03,427 --> 00:06:04,981
A mirror is the best,

176
00:06:04,981 --> 00:06:08,088
because it doubles the candlelight and the

177
00:06:08,088 --> 00:06:08,976
tree lights.

178
00:06:09,156 --> 00:06:11,065
My mother hung her wreath on a

179
00:06:11,065 --> 00:06:13,102
ribbon from the top of the wall,

180
00:06:13,102 --> 00:06:15,265
so it floated over the mantel like

181
00:06:15,265 --> 00:06:15,902
a picture.

182
00:06:16,252 --> 00:06:19,047
So far, a triangle not a line,

183
00:06:19,047 --> 00:06:20,351
a fat garland,

184
00:06:20,351 --> 00:06:23,705
one idea, and something on the wall.

185
00:06:23,885 --> 00:06:25,847
Mistake number five.

186
00:06:26,027 --> 00:06:30,358
Mismatched, saggy stockings hanging every which way.

187
00:06:30,538 --> 00:06:32,333
Hang them evenly spaced,

188
00:06:32,333 --> 00:06:33,754
at the same height.

189
00:06:33,934 --> 00:06:36,425
And if your stockings don't match,

190
00:06:36,425 --> 00:06:38,624
tie the same red ribbon or the

191
00:06:38,624 --> 00:06:40,749
same little tag on every one.

192
00:06:40,929 --> 00:06:42,856
Suddenly they look like a set.

193
00:06:43,206 --> 00:06:45,115
And please, honey,

194
00:06:45,115 --> 00:06:46,282
be careful.

195
00:06:46,462 --> 00:06:48,325
If your fireplace works,

196
00:06:48,325 --> 00:06:51,275
never hang stockings or garland over a

197
00:06:51,275 --> 00:06:54,380
burning fire, and never use real candles

198
00:06:54,380 --> 00:06:55,855
near a dry garland.

199
00:06:56,035 --> 00:06:58,466
A Christmas fire is the most common

200
00:06:58,466 --> 00:07:00,551
way a house burns in December.

201
00:07:00,731 --> 00:07:03,465
My neighbor lost her whole living room

202
00:07:03,465 --> 00:07:06,560
in nineteen seventy-eight to one candle and

203
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:07,999
one dry pine branch.

204
00:07:08,349 --> 00:07:11,030
And here's the stocking holder trick.

205
00:07:11,210 --> 00:07:14,262
If you don't have proper stocking hangers,

206
00:07:14,262 --> 00:07:16,079
take a long wooden board,

207
00:07:16,079 --> 00:07:18,550
paint it, and screw cup hooks into

208
00:07:18,550 --> 00:07:19,349
the bottom.

209
00:07:19,529 --> 00:07:21,543
Lay it on the mantel and set

210
00:07:21,543 --> 00:07:23,413
a few heavy things on top,

211
00:07:23,413 --> 00:07:25,787
like your candlesticks and books.

212
00:07:25,967 --> 00:07:27,761
It holds every stocking,

213
00:07:27,761 --> 00:07:30,900
nothing falls, and it doesn't scratch your

214
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:31,423
mantel.

215
00:07:31,603 --> 00:07:34,364
My son-in-law made ours in twenty minutes

216
00:07:34,364 --> 00:07:35,644
in nineteen ninety.

217
00:07:35,994 --> 00:07:37,967
Mistake number six.

218
00:07:38,147 --> 00:07:40,620
A mantel with nothing alive on it.

219
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:42,890
All plastic and glitter.

220
00:07:43,070 --> 00:07:44,929
Add one living thing,

221
00:07:44,929 --> 00:07:45,903
sweetheart.

222
00:07:46,083 --> 00:07:49,008
A bowl of red apples or oranges.

223
00:07:49,188 --> 00:07:51,000
A potted amaryllis.

224
00:07:51,180 --> 00:07:53,777
Fresh cranberries in a glass jar with

225
00:07:53,777 --> 00:07:55,742
water and a floating candle.

226
00:07:55,922 --> 00:07:58,541
It makes the mantel look like a

227
00:07:58,541 --> 00:08:01,414
real home, where real people live.

228
00:08:01,594 --> 00:08:04,665
And remember those extra things you took

229
00:08:04,665 --> 00:08:04,972
off?

230
00:08:05,152 --> 00:08:07,004
Put them on a side table,

231
00:08:07,004 --> 00:08:08,264
grouped together.

232
00:08:08,444 --> 00:08:10,789
They'll look better there anyway.

233
00:08:11,139 --> 00:08:13,327
And now mistake number seven,

234
00:08:13,327 --> 00:08:15,214
the trick I promised you.

235
00:08:15,394 --> 00:08:17,832
Only decorating for the daytime.

236
00:08:18,012 --> 00:08:21,027
Most people see your mantel at night,

237
00:08:21,027 --> 00:08:22,087
by lamplight.

238
00:08:22,267 --> 00:08:25,182
So my mother put little votive candles

239
00:08:25,182 --> 00:08:26,716
in plain glass jars,

240
00:08:26,716 --> 00:08:28,327
all along the mantel,

241
00:08:28,327 --> 00:08:30,475
tucked down in the greenery.

242
00:08:30,655 --> 00:08:33,205
At night, she turned off the overhead

243
00:08:33,205 --> 00:08:34,514
light and lit them,

244
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:36,857
and the whole mantel glowed like a

245
00:08:36,857 --> 00:08:38,167
church at midnight.

246
00:08:38,517 --> 00:08:41,965
Today, honey, use the little battery candles

247
00:08:41,965 --> 00:08:42,905
with timers.

248
00:08:43,085 --> 00:08:44,180
They look real,

249
00:08:44,180 --> 00:08:46,369
they're safe near the garland,

250
00:08:46,369 --> 00:08:48,777
and they come on by themselves at

251
00:08:48,777 --> 00:08:50,748
five o'clock every evening.

252
00:08:50,928 --> 00:08:52,956
Get a dozen of them for about

253
00:08:52,956 --> 00:08:53,795
ten dollars.

254
00:08:53,975 --> 00:08:54,909
Tuck them in,

255
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:55,915
set the timer,

256
00:08:55,915 --> 00:08:58,572
and every night your living room will

257
00:08:58,572 --> 00:09:00,512
look like a Christmas card.

258
00:09:00,692 --> 00:09:03,488
It's the cheapest trick there is,

259
00:09:03,488 --> 00:09:05,521
and nobody ever does it.

260
00:09:05,872 --> 00:09:07,671
And one last thing.

261
00:09:07,851 --> 00:09:09,656
Don't forget the hearth,

262
00:09:09,656 --> 00:09:12,439
sweetheart, the floor in front of the

263
00:09:12,439 --> 00:09:13,192
fireplace.

264
00:09:13,372 --> 00:09:16,476
That's where a big basket of pinecones,

265
00:09:16,476 --> 00:09:18,943
a stack of firewood tied with a

266
00:09:18,943 --> 00:09:21,650
red ribbon, or a big lantern goes.

267
00:09:21,830 --> 00:09:24,302
It grounds the whole picture.

268
00:09:24,482 --> 00:09:27,333
A beautiful mantel floating above an empty

269
00:09:27,333 --> 00:09:28,894
floor looks unfinished.

270
00:09:29,074 --> 00:09:30,775
Fill that bottom corner,

271
00:09:30,775 --> 00:09:33,823
and suddenly the whole wall looks complete.

272
00:09:34,173 --> 00:09:36,379
My mother put an old milk can

273
00:09:36,379 --> 00:09:37,444
on our hearth,

274
00:09:37,444 --> 00:09:40,715
painted red, filled with tall pine branches

275
00:09:40,715 --> 00:09:43,225
and a few branches of red berries

276
00:09:43,225 --> 00:09:44,366
from the hedge.

277
00:09:44,546 --> 00:09:47,382
When the minister came for his Christmas

278
00:09:47,382 --> 00:09:49,508
visit, he sat on our couch and

279
00:09:49,508 --> 00:09:51,210
stared at that milk can,

280
00:09:51,210 --> 00:09:53,691
and he asked her where she'd bought

281
00:09:53,691 --> 00:09:53,904
it.

282
00:09:54,084 --> 00:09:55,548
She said, Reverend,

283
00:09:55,548 --> 00:09:57,474
I bought it from the cow.

284
00:09:57,654 --> 00:09:59,407
He laughed for ten minutes.

285
00:09:59,757 --> 00:10:01,126
So one more time.

286
00:10:01,306 --> 00:10:02,794
Build a triangle,

287
00:10:02,794 --> 00:10:03,756
not a line,

288
00:10:03,756 --> 00:10:05,068
in odd numbers.

289
00:10:05,248 --> 00:10:08,307
Layer real greenery into your garland and

290
00:10:08,307 --> 00:10:09,277
let it drape.

291
00:10:09,457 --> 00:10:11,187
Pick one idea.

292
00:10:11,367 --> 00:10:13,921
Hang something on the wall above.

293
00:10:14,101 --> 00:10:15,935
Space the stockings evenly.

294
00:10:16,115 --> 00:10:18,019
Add one living thing.

295
00:10:18,199 --> 00:10:20,541
And put little candles in the greenery

296
00:10:20,541 --> 00:10:21,404
for the night.

297
00:10:21,584 --> 00:10:24,370
That's a mantel your family will remember.

298
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:26,773
Tell me in the comments,

299
00:10:26,773 --> 00:10:27,715
sweetheart.

300
00:10:27,895 --> 00:10:30,598
What's the one thing that always goes

301
00:10:30,598 --> 00:10:32,643
on your mantel at Christmas?

302
00:10:32,823 --> 00:10:34,542
I'd love to hear it.

303
00:10:34,722 --> 00:10:37,746
The whole playlist of Grandma's Christmas tips

304
00:10:37,746 --> 00:10:39,719
is right there on your screen,

305
00:10:39,719 --> 00:10:41,560
and I'll see you in the next

306
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:41,955
video.

307
00:10:42,135 --> 00:10:43,725
Good night, honey.
